.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt PCI_BRIDGE 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pci_scan_bridge
.Nd scan buses behind a PCI-to-PCI bridge
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/pci.h
.Ft int
.Fn pci_scan_bridge "pci_device_t *bridge"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn pci_scan_bridge
function inspects a previously discovered PCI bridge device and scans the bus
range described by its secondary and subordinate bus-number registers.
.Pp
Only devices with class code
.Dv 0x0604
are treated as PCI-to-PCI bridges.
Non-bridge devices, disabled bridges, and bridges with invalid secondary or
subordinate bus ranges are ignored.
.Pp
The bridge scan shares the same device-recording logic as
.Fn pci_scan_bus ,
so newly discovered downstream functions become visible through
.Fn pci_find_device .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn pci_scan_bridge
function returns the number of downstream functions discovered behind the
bridge.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pci_config 9 ,
.Xr pci_scan 9 ,
.Xr bus 9
